* Create a library.  c.link reads a library once, in order, so each
* member must follow one that refers to it.  docmd.r and setbuf.r refer
* to members that refer back to them, so no order works for them, and
* makeed links them directly instead.
merge >objs.1 subst.r set.r move.r join.r gettxt.r getrhs.r maksub.r getfn.r
merge >objs.2 dowrite.r doread.r egets.r doprnt.r doglob.r getlst.r getone.r
merge >objs.3 getnum.r find.r del.r ckglob.r optpat.r getpat.r makepat.r unmkpat.r
merge >objs.4 dodash.r esc.r matchs.r deflt.r catsub.r append.r ins.r getptr.r
merge >objs.5 amatch.r omatch.r bitmap.r
merge >objs.l objs.1 objs.2 objs.3 objs.4 objs.5
del objs.1 objs.2 objs.3 objs.4 objs.5
